25. What has not been demonstrated
Several stronger interpretations should presently be excluded.
This addendum has not demonstrated that:

the Navier–Stokes singularity is the quantum horizon;
the singular vortex becomes an atmosphere;
\(r=\lambda_n\);
\(Re_\theta=\nu_n\);
\(Re_\theta=K_n\);
molecules are the primitive R²D constituents;

or

the full Navier–Stokes equation has already been derived from R²D.

It has also not established that the physical replacement boundary occurs precisely at
\[
c_B=1.
\]
Ordinary kinetic theory predicts loss of hydrodynamic validity substantially before literal one-particle occupancy in many systems.
The stronger R²D claim is independent of the exact threshold:

for every finite threshold, the shrinking support crosses it before \(\tau=0\).

40. What Has Not Been Derived
This addendum does not yet derive:
\[
\mu_n=f(\mathcal W_n)
\]
for a specific function \(f\);
the numerical value of the background mass scale
\[
m_n^\Phi;
\]
the exact relation between background recurrence and physical mass calibration;
Newton’s second law;
the equivalence principle quantitatively;
the Einstein field equations;
the Standard Model masses of elementary particles;
mass generation through the Higgs mechanism;
or an exact count formula for binding-energy mass defects.
These remain empirical and theoretical burdens.
The purpose of the addendum is prior to all of them.
It establishes which boundary owns the mass whose later physical behavior those theories describe.

2. These Coordinates Have Different Readability Regimes
The central R²D classification is:

\[
\boxed{
\begin{array}{c|cc}
& \lambda & \nu \\ \hline
\text{Thermodynamic} & \text{readable} & \text{readable} \\
\text{Quantum} & \text{unreadable} & \text{readable} \\
\text{Gravitational} & \text{readable} & \text{unreadable}
\end{array}
}
\]
This table is not a taxonomy added after the physical theories have been constructed.
It predicts that different physical coordinate systems should appear when opposite parts of closure remain readable.

44. R²D Does Not Need to Interpret This as a Smallest Possible Material Object
The equality does not by itself prove:

discrete Planck-sized spatial cells;
infinite density;
a singular primitive point;
or a new fundamental particle.

55. This Explains Why Their Conventional Mathematical Languages Look So Different
Quantum mechanics is naturally expressed through:

phase;
frequency;
complex recurrence;
amplitudes.

Gravity is naturally expressed through:

area;
radius;
metric geometry;
curvature.

R²D proposes that this difference reflects opposite readability horizons rather than unrelated primitive ontologies.

21. Closure Completeness Is Not Conventional Equilibrium
The phrase “closed subordinate dynamics” might be mistaken for thermodynamic equilibrium.

That would be incorrect.
A subordinate boundary can repeatedly cycle while:
    • consuming free energy;
    • producing heat;
    • carrying chemical flux;
    • exchanging matter;
    • or participating in a nonequilibrium steady state.
Thus:

closure complete is not detailed-balance equilibrium.

Closure is boundary relative.

29. Observable Replacement Requires State Ownership
A practical criterion for direct recursive replacement is therefore:

a subordinate recurrence is independently measurable;
an enclosing state is independently measurable;
multiple subordinate realizations map to that state;
subordinate path identity is unnecessary to specify it;
the experimental read can be shifted between the boundaries.

[Editorial source note: on PDF page 1130 this numbered criterion is printed in one oversized box and clipped at the right edge. The full five-item list is retained from the supplied Markdown pending author confirmation.]
Muscle satisfies these criteria across directly accessible scales.

33. The Same Biological State Can Contain Vast Subordinate Activity
A muscle can maintain a stable functional state while:

Myosin switches continue to transition;
protein conformations fluctuate;
molecular vibrations recur;
still faster subordinate dynamics remain active.

Thus:

stable function is not static subordinate structure.

The stability belongs to the enclosing boundary.
The activity belongs to subordinate boundaries.

2. A Folded Protein Is Not One Microscopic Configuration
Even a stable folded protein is not microscopically static.
Its subordinate molecular coordinates continue to change.

Among the possible dynamics are:

bond vibration;
side-chain rotation;
local backbone fluctuation;
loop motion;
hydration rearrangement;
packing fluctuation;
domain breathing;
and larger conformational recurrence.

Therefore the folded state cannot generally be identified with one instantaneous subordinate configuration.
If it were, any local fluctuation would destroy the fold.
Experimentally, it does not.
The structural state persists while subordinate coordinates change.
Thus:

persistent structure is not persistent microscopic configuration.

15. Sequence Is Essential but Is Not the Fold
The amino-acid sequence strongly constrains the physical interactions available to the protein.
Sequence affects:

local chemistry;
steric compatibility;
charge distribution;
hydrophobicity;
hydrogen bonding;
packing;
flexibility;
interaction with the environment.

Thus sequence constrains which structural realizations are physically admissible.
But:

sequence is not the folded state.

The sequence belongs to one physical description.
The folded structure belongs to an enclosing structural boundary.

16. The Environment Also Constrains the Folding Landscape
Protein structure is not realized in the absence of an enclosing physical relation.

Relevant conditions can include:
 • solvent;
 • ionic environment;
 • pH;
 • temperature;
 • membrane environment;
 • ligands;
 • binding partners;
 • chaperones;
 • mechanical constraint;
 • covalent modification;
 • and crowding.
Therefore the admissible structural landscape should be represented schematically as
\[\mathcal M_{\mathrm{fold}}=\mathcal M_{\mathrm{fold}}(\text{sequence},\text{environment}).\]
The precise physical variables depend on the protein and experiment.

36. This Does Not Derive Folding Kinetics From R²D Alone
R²D does not, from the replacement map alone, calculate:

folding rates;
transition-state barriers;
pathway probabilities;
solvent friction;
specific contact formation;
atomistic mechanisms.

Those remain physical bridge problems.
The R²D result concerns state ownership.
It identifies what a folded state is relative to the trajectories that realize it.

32. This Is Not Subjectivity
The word “context” should not imply observer dependence.

The relevant context is physical:

chemical environment;
binding partners;
mechanical load;
substrate availability;
membrane geometry;
electrical or chemical gradients;
cellular network state;
tissue constraint;
other enclosing relations.

Thus:

functional context = physical enclosing relation.

36. Internal Energy Contributes to Enclosing Mass
The same reasoning applies to internal energetic organization such as:
 • thermal excitation;
 • internal kinetic energy;
 • radiation;
 • chemical energy;
 • field energy;
 • binding organization.
If such a contribution changes the zero-momentum energy of the enclosing boundary by
\[\Delta E_{\mathrm{internal}},\]
then the enclosing invariant mass changes by
\[\Delta M=\frac{\Delta E_{\mathrm{internal}}}{c^2}.\]
This is why physical mass cannot be reduced to static multiplicity cardinality alone.
The boundary class and its realized physical energetic organization occupy different roles.

4. Specify the Physical Regime Assume:

four-dimensional metric geometry;
spherical symmetry;
a vacuum exterior,

\[T_{\mu\nu}=0;\]

vanishing local cosmological term for the Schwarzschild problem,

\[\Lambda=0;\]

static exterior geometry;
asymptotic flatness.

These are the physical projection assumptions defining the Schwarzschild exterior problem.

53. Conditional Theorem — Area-First Schwarzschild Projection Assume:

the four-dimensional metric projection established in Addendum 39;
vanishing exterior stress-energy;
\(\Lambda=0\);
spherical symmetry;
staticity;
asymptotic flatness;
areal radius defined by

\[A_G=4\pi r_A^2;\]

weak-field matching to the Keplerian calibration

\[g_G=\mu_G/r_A^2.\]
Then the unique static spherical exterior metric has
\[N^2=1-\frac{2\mu_G}{c^2r_A},\]
and

\[H^2=\left(1-\frac{2\mu_G}{c^2r_A}\right)^{-1}.\]
Therefore,
\[ds^2=-\left(1-\frac{2\mu_G}{c^2r_A}\right)c^2dt^2+\left(1-\frac{2\mu_G}{c^2r_A}\right)^{-1}dr_A^2+r_A^2d\Omega^2.\]
After \(\mu_G=GM\), this is the Schwarzschild exterior solution.

2. The Test Requires Two Coupled Gravitational Boundaries
A useful test system must contain:

a subordinate gravitational horizon;
an enclosing gravitational horizon;
a continuously varying gravitational source coordinate;
a regime in which both boundaries remain separately readable;
and a known limiting mass at which the two-horizon classification becomes marginal.

Schwarzschild–de Sitter possesses exactly this architecture.

60. The Real Cosmological Peers Need Not Be Coins or Binary
The toy example supplies only a finite exact demonstration.
The actual peer-boundary realization domain may have:
 • many states;
 • many compatibility classes;
 • nonuniform multiplicities;
 • changing constraints;
 • large radix.
The general architecture does not require a binary system.

57. Principle — Physical Branch Orientation Requires a Projection Bridge
The sign of the physical rate depends on:

• the sign of the realized structural transition;



the orientation of the macrostate-to-area projection;
the orientation of the physical clock coordinate.

Therefore the bridge from R²D direction to Friedmann branch must be explicitly derived.

15. The General Source Is More Than Rest Mass
A relativistic source can carry:

rest energy;
kinetic energy;
momentum;
pressure;
stress;
energy flux;
momentum flux.

Therefore scalar rest-mass summation is only one physical limit of the source projection.

39. The Second Friedmann Equation Is Therefore Not Independent in This Construction
Within a fixed FLRW projection with source continuity and constant G, k , and Λ, the acceleration equation follows from:
1. the first Friedmann rate constraint;
2. source-support continuity;
3. the kinematic identity ä/a = Ḣ + H 2 .
Thus it need not be introduced as a second primitive cosmological postulate.

9. Structural Geometry Can Therefore Be Followed Alongside Recurrence
At an appropriate thermodynamic structural boundary, one may read:

a structural distinction;
its state occupancy;
a physical displacement or configuration;
and its recurrence.

The distinction and recurrence remain physically coordinated.

31. Cross-Scale Spectroscopy Can Potentially Answer That Question
Different spectral regions may respond differently to perturbations that alter:

enclosing structure;
local chemistry;
temperature;
binding;
mechanical constraint;
or recursive organization.

Those differential responses can help assign boundary ownership.

15. No Complex Number Has Yet Been Introduced
At this stage there is only:

a boundary;
an ordered recurrent relation;
and closure modulo Kn .

42. This Matters for Nonspatial Quantum Degrees of Freedom
A state can carry phase without being represented as a literal spatial wave.

This will become important for:

stationary states;
spin;
internal state recurrence;
relative phase between alternatives;
and gauge structure.

69. They Cannot Be Assumed to Be Primitive Objects
The alternatives may correspond to:

boundary macrostates;
recurrence classes;
orientation classes;
detector distinctions;
or another complete boundary classification.

The mapping must be derived for each physical representation.

39. The Equation Is Already Schrödinger-Like
But it contains:

no ℏ;
no joules;


• no physical time unit; - no spatial kinetic operator.
Those come later.

6. Gauge Transformation Is Not an R2D Occurrence
It need not represent:

macrostate transition;
occupancy change;
closure;
recursive carry;


• or background change.
It can alter only the physical mathematical representation.

38. Therefore the Maxwell Functional Requires Additional Conditions
Select the leading theory to be:

local;
gauge invariant;
Lorentz invariant;
parity even;
lowest nontrivial order in curvature;
and linear in the resulting bulk field equation.

68. This Convergence Is the Central Consistency Check
The same conserved-current structure is required by:

source ontology;
gauge representation;
and curvature dynamics.

79. What Has Been Derived Is Its Position in the Architecture
It must occur after:

closure phase;
local phase comparison;
connection;
curvature;
retained charge orientation;
and conserved source current.

22. The Detector Statistics Are Not Uniquely Quantum
The same binary occupancy form appears in:

molecular switches;
chemical states;
muscle;
thermal detectors;
and other binary count domains.

The specifically quantum content lies in the conditional bridge to \(A_{D\mid q}\).

27. This Is Not Observer Subjectivity
The boundary is physical.
It may be defined by:

detector geometry;
coupling;
orientation;
field configuration;



threshold;
amplification architecture;
or environmental relation.

No conscious observer is required.

64. A Different Detector Defines a Different Count Classification
Changing:

orientation;
basis;
coupling;
threshold;
interaction channel;
or detector geometry

changes which macrostates can become readable.

5. A Physical Test Must Identify What Can Fail
A discriminating test requires a specified mapping and observable consequences. It should identify:

which quantities are measured independently;
which parameters are calibrated and which are fitted;
which preparations or constraints are varied;
what outcome the mapping predicts;
what uncertainty and auxiliary assumptions enter the prediction;
which outcomes would challenge the mapping in its stated domain.

Independent determination of every primitive count is not always operationally available. In that case, the proposed bridge must explain how measurable consequences follow and where calibration or inference enters. An unavailable measurement must be reported rather than silently replaced by the observation the mapping was constructed to explain.
If evidence contradicts a prediction, the immediate target is the combination of mapping and auxiliary assumptions that generated it. Further analysis identifies which element failed.
A critic need not establish a rival universal ontology before demonstrating such a conflict. A successful rival fit, however, is not itself a contradiction unless the compared claims make incompatible consequences in the tested conditions.
The scope of failure matters. Failure of a physical assignment does not erase a valid conditional implication whose premises remain explicitly hypothetical.

10. Machine Experience Remains a Boundary Question
The experience postulate directs a machine inquiry toward:

the proposed experiencing boundary;
the readable states and candidate closure;
the recurrence of completed realizations;
the enclosing relations sustaining that recurrence;
any survey participating in subsequent organization;
the observational bridge supporting those identifications.

Persistent computation alone does not specify all of these.
An AI can generate follow-up questions or operate within a recurring task. Those achievements do not, by themselves, establish that the inquiry maintains an experiential closure.
If machine experience were established under the postulate, its content would have to be investigated at the machine boundary. Human language would not make that content human.
Ask R²D should therefore avoid both promotion of fluency into human consciousness and categorical exclusion of every possible machine experience from a human resemblance test.

16. Conclusion
Experience is proposed here as sustained closure within enclosing relations. Surveying is a boundary-specific retained read that can participate in subsequent realization.
Human narratives are one form of that survey. Their usefulness can become lived constraint without establishing their account of enclosing agency.
AI can survey human surveys without thereby realizing human experience. Other candidate boundaries need not survey through human protagonists or rulers.
The central direction for Ask R²D is
\[
\boxed{
\text{Define the sustained organization and its local read before assigning experience.}
}
\]
The companion representational principle is
\[
\boxed{
\text{A survey belongs within the world it reads; it does not independently define that world.}
}
\]

11. Institutional Surveys Become Part of Institutional Constraint
An institution can retain records, classifications, indicators, and evaluations. These are candidate surveys of its activity.
Addendum 88 supplies the relevant ordering: a retained read can participate in organizing subsequent realization without independently defining the enclosing relation it represents.
For example, suppose an illustrative office measures the number of requests closed. Participants may then organize activity around that measure.
Closing more records does not, by definition alone, establish that more needs were met, that the service remained adequate, or that the supporting organization became more persistent.
The distinction is:
\[
\boxed{
\text{A measure can constrain institutional activity without completely measuring its sustaining function.}
}
\]
Ask R²D should identify:

the activity represented by the indicator;
the domain omitted from that read;
how the indicator enters subsequent decisions;
the evidence connecting improvement in the indicator to the intended outcome.

The survey can be useful and accurate within its domain. Its practical influence does not make it an exhaustive ruler of institutional organization.
Calling these records surveys also does not establish institutional experience. That separate proposal requires the boundary and sustained-closure account discussed in Addendum 88.

11. What Would Make the Comparison Discriminating?
Agreement with a frequency update can support a prediction without distinguishing ontologies.
A rigorous biological comparison should specify:

native classifications and the conditions under which they remain fixed;
the enclosing compatibility or constraint relation;
how compatible counts are measured or inferred;
which realization law connects them to reproduction or persistence;
predictions fixed before observing the outcome;
which rival claim gives a different consequence.

Defining \(\Theta_i\) after the fact solely to reproduce measured \(w_i\) does not independently establish the bridge. Multiplicity can be inferred rather than directly enumerated, but the inference must preserve possible-count meaning instead of substituting the number that survived.
Changing enclosing conditions while holding the selected native description fixed can test a claim that this native description is sufficient. It does not automatically refute a wider model that already includes those enclosing conditions.
Likewise, the fixed-landscape theorem does not refute a theory explicitly describing changes in the state architecture. That theory must instead be examined for how it defines and realizes those changes.
The formal R²D conflict concerns causal ordering under its premises. Universal physical applicability requires the additional mapping and evidence appropriate to that scope.
